<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32439" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏlĕa</span></b> , ae
			(<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>dat.
			plur.</i> oleabus, Gell. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. 1,
			40</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαία</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>an olive</i>, <i>olive-berry</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olea ab elaea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 108</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleas caducas, et albas condire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleam cogere, legere, stringere, verberare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 144</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 2, 3, § 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G.
				2, 302 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an olive-tree</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Stich. 5, 4, 9</span></i>: agricola cum florem oleae videt, bacam
			quoque se visurum putat. <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 2, 6, 16</span></i>; so <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 3,
				9, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 6, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ure maris oleas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 741</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Isa. 17, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 13</span></i>.
				</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
